    "question": {
      "text": "If the vector $e^{px-y-z}(\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j+\\mathbf k)$ is solenoidal, then the value of $p$ is ______.",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$-3$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$3$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$-2$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$2$"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "D",
      "correctText": "$2$",
      "explanation": "Given $\\mathbf V=e^{px-y-z}(\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j+\\mathbf k)$ is solenoidal. We know that if $\\mathbf V$ is solenoidal, $\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf V=0$. Thus $\\frac{\\partial V_1}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial V_2}{\\partial y}+\\frac{\\partial V_3}{\\partial z}=0$, giving $e^{px-y-z}(p-1-1)=0$. Hence $p=2$. Choice (D).",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
