    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "A",
      "correctText": "$15\\sqrt{37}$",
      "explanation": "Let $x=t$, $y=\\frac t6$, $z=4$ and $3\\le t\\le6$. Then $ds=\\sqrt{(dx/dt)^2+(dy/dt)^2}\\,dt=\\frac{\\sqrt{37}}6dt$. Substituting and integrating from $3$ to $6$ gives $15\\sqrt{37}$. Choice (A).",
      "status": "confirmed"
