    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "$\\frac{-\\mathbf i+3\\mathbf j-3\\mathbf k}{\\sqrt{19}}$",
      "explanation": "Let $f(x,y,z)=xy^3+3yz-3$. The normal vector is $\\nabla f=y^3\\mathbf i+(3xy^2+3z)\\mathbf j+3y\\mathbf k$. At $(3,-1,-2)$, $\\nabla f=-\\mathbf i+3\\mathbf j-3\\mathbf k$. Therefore the unit normal vector is $\\frac{-\\mathbf i+3\\mathbf j-3\\mathbf k}{\\sqrt{19}}$. Choice (B).",
      "status": "confirmed"
