    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "$\\frac{2590}{3}$",
      "explanation": "Let $f(x,y,z)=x^2+y^2-49$. Then $\\nabla f=2x\\mathbf i+2y\\mathbf j$ and $\\hat n=\\frac{1}{7}(x\\mathbf i+y\\mathbf j)$. Consider the projection of $S$ on the $yz$-plane, a rectangle with sides $7$ and $5$. Thus $dA=\\frac{dy\\,dz}{\\hat n\\cdot\\mathbf i}=\\frac{7}{x}dy\\,dz$. Hence $\\mathbf F\\cdot\\hat n=\\frac{xz^2+xy^2}{7}$ and the surface integral becomes $\\int_0^5\\int_0^7(z^2+y^2)\\,dy\\,dz=\\frac{2590}{3}$. Choice (C).",
      "status": "confirmed"
